course: dictionary
lesson: 8001
title: Redness: a colour and a warning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Redness is a noun. It is the state of being red, like the redness of a ripe tomato. It is uncountable, so you say «some redness» or «redness and swelling», never «a redness» or «rednesses».
explain: On the body, redness of the skin is a red patch. The clues around the word tell you more. «Redness, heat, swelling and yellow pus are signs of infection» shows that redness can be a warning, not just a colour. Skin can be red because it is sore, hot, sunburnt or infected.
explain: Look for the clues in the sentence. «Limping, swelling or redness need a doctor» tells you redness is a reason to get help. So when redness comes with swelling or heat, think: this could be a problem, and an adult should check it.
fact: Redness means the state of being red.
fact: Redness of the skin is a red patch that can mean it is sore, hot, sunburnt or infected.
fact: «Redness and swelling» around a cut can be a sign of infection.
fact: Redness can also be a sign of sunburn after time in the sun.
fact: Redness is uncountable, so you say «some redness», not «a redness».
exercise: «Redness, heat, swelling and yellow pus are signs of infection.» In this sentence, redness is | A type of bandage | *A warning sign of infection | A happy feeling | A kind of fruit
exercise: Mia says redness is just a colour, like a sunset. Why is that only half the story? | Redness is a kind of cloud | Redness is always a happy colour | Redness only means blue | *On skin, it can be a warning sign of infection or sunburn
exercise: «Limping, swelling or redness need a doctor.» What should you do if you see redness with swelling? | Cover it up and forget about it | *Tell an adult, so a doctor can check it | Wait a year to see what happens | Ignore it, it will go away by itself
test: Which phrase is correct? | *some redness | three rednesses | a rednesses
test: A cut has «redness and swelling» around it. What might this suggest? | *A possible infection, so tell an adult | The cut is certainly healed | Nothing at all is wrong | A new kind of paint
exam: Which sentence uses redness correctly? | *The sunburn caused some redness on her shoulders | Redness is a loud sound | She has three rednesses on her face | The rednesses are on her shoulders
